{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward if recent sentiment is positive (0.25 or above) and model overestimates prices — indicates bullish sentiment may be overblown.",
    "Apply a mild upward bias to forecasts when the model has consistently underestimated recent price peaks — suggests mean reversion or lagged momentum correction.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp price spikes (e.g., >65.0) by 5–10% to avoid overreacting to short-term volatility.",
    "If sentiment is neutral (0.00) and model shows persistent underperformance, apply a 2–3% upward adjustment to correct for mean reversion bias.",
    "For 30-day forecasts, if the last 3–5 true values show a clear upward trend, slightly increase forecasted peak to account for momentum, but cap at +10% above recent high."
  ]
}
